# ==============================================================================
# sudoers-lab02-deploy.example - Least-Privilege Sudoers Rule Example
# Part of "30 Days of DevOps" by Ahmad Jawad Bandesha
#
# LEAST PRIVILEGE RATIONALE:
# 1. Why avoid ALL:
#    Granting "ALL=(ALL) ALL" completely destroys the boundary between a service
#    account and root. Any compromise of the service account immediately yields
#    full cluster/root compromise.
#
# 2. Why avoid wildcards (*):
#    Wildcards allow flag injection and command hijacking. For instance, allowing
#    "/usr/bin/systemctl *" allows an attacker to run:
#      sudo systemctl edit --stdin (launching interactive editor)
#      sudo systemctl start malicious.service
#      sudo systemctl status ../../../bin/bash
#
# 3. Specific, exact command only:
#    This rule allows lab02_deploy to run ONLY the status check for one single
#    specific unit file without a password prompt.
# ==============================================================================

lab02_deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl status lab02-demo.service
